From: Mansour Ayouni <kalidianow@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Free the stack when entering a Catch block

Each statement ends by freeing the stack, so an EMPTY Catch block never
cleans up, and every caught error leaves one value behind. After about
1003 of them (RING_VM_STACK_SIZE) the program aborts with
Error (R4) : Stack Overflow, from code that contains no recursion.

Emitting ICO_FREESTACK on entry to the Catch block fixes it. A non-empty
Catch block is unaffected: its first statement already frees the stack.

---
 language/src/stmt.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/language/src/stmt.c b/language/src/stmt.c
--- a/language/src/stmt.c
+++ b/language/src/stmt.c
@@ -998,6 +998,12 @@ int ring_parser_stmt(Parser *pParser) {
 			nMark1 = ring_parser_icg_newlabel(pParser);
 			ring_parser_icg_addoperandint(pParser, pMark, nMark1);
 			RING_STATE_PRINTRULE(RING_RULE_CATCH);
+			/*
+			**  Free the stack on entry to the Catch block
+			**  An empty Catch block contains no statement, so nothing would
+			**  clean the stack and each caught error would leave one value
+			*/
+			ring_parser_icg_freestack(pParser);
 			RING_PARSER_ACCEPTSTATEMENTS;
 			if (ring_parser_iskeyword(pParser, K_DONE) || ring_parser_iskeyword(pParser, K_ENDTRY) ||
 			    ring_parser_iskeyword(pParser, K_END) || ring_parser_csbraceend(pParser)) {
